  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the 13 files that make up the export-tracking system's full surface area:\n\n1. **`zerver/lib/export.py`** \u2014 core export logic (`get_realm_exports_serialized`, `export_realm_wrapper`, `do_export_realm`); the module the migration's backfill would read from and that all callers depend on.\n2. **`zerver/actions/realm_export.py`** \u2014 actions layer (`notify_realm_export`, `do_delete_realm_export`) that creates/updates export tracking state.\n3. **`zerver/views/realm_export.py`** \u2014 HTTP views (`export_realm`, `get_realm_exports`, `delete_realm_export`, `get_users_export_consents`) serving export status to the frontend.\n4. **`zerver/worker/deferred_work.py`** \u2014 background worker (`DeferredWorker.consume`, `realm_export` event branch) that runs the actual export job and writes progress/failure state.\n5. **`zerver/models/realm_audit_logs.py`** \u2014 defines `AuditLogEventType.REALM_EXPORTED` and the `extra_data` JSON field currently used as the ad hoc tracking store the new `RealmExport` model replaces.\n6. **`zerver/models/__init__.py`** \u2014 model registration point; where a new `RealmExport` import would need to be added.\n7. **`zerver/models/realms.py`** \u2014 defines `EXPORT_PUBLIC`, `EXPORT_FULL_WITH_CONSENT`, `EXPORT_FULL_WITHOUT_CONSENT` export-type constants used throughout.\n8. **`zerver/management/commands/export.py`** \u2014 CLI export command that also writes a `RealmAuditLog` tracking row.\n9. **`zerver/tests/test_realm_export.py`** \u2014 dedicated export endpoint tests (S3 + local uploads, rate limiting, failure/retry, delete).\n10. **`zerver/tests/test_import_export.py`** \u2014 import/export round-trip tests.\n11. **`zerver/tests/test_management_commands.py`** \u2014 `TestExport` management-command test.\n12. **`zerver/tests/test_events.py`** \u2014 event-system tests likely covering the `realm_export` event payload.\n13. **`zerver/lib/event_schema.py`** \u2014 schema checker module used to validate the `realm_export` event shape.\n\nNote: `zerver/migrations/0595_add_realmexport_table_and_backfill.py` referenced in the task does not exist in this repository snapshot \u2014 it appears to be the not-yet-created migration this task is asking about, so I could not retrieve it directly. The files above are what it would touch/depend on (model registration, `extra_data`-based tracking to backfill from, and all direct/indirect consumers).",
